WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.434
[music playing]

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.705
OK, this is going to be tight.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.340
BEAR GRYLLS (VOICEOVER):
Comedian and actor

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.744
Joel McHale and I are trying
to navigate a deep slop

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.645
canyon in the Arizona desert.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.047
Oh my god.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:18.051
BEAR GRYLLS (VOICEOVER): But it
just became dangerously narrow.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.052
Oh, I'm stuck.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.855
[grunts]

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.390
Keep going.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.659
Wriggle, keep wriggling.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.627
[grunts]

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.937
I'm fine, Bear.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.439
You go ahead.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:43.009
JOEL MCHALE: I'm, you
know, a larger man,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.645
and there's a lot
of tight crevices.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:50.784
This is not a hike for those
that enjoy pizza all the time.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.218
So now this is--

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.254
this is all from flash
flood here, like barbed wire

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.388
and everything.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.725
Yeah, it's going
to get very tight.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.894
Yeah, you think?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.263
BEAR GRYLLS: It's been getting
progressively narrower.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.897
You know, it kind of
gives you that little bit

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.399
of claustrophobic feeling.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.701
And this is one of the ones
where you just got to take

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.404
your time with because
the danger of slot canyons

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.807
is you get caught in
them, you get committed,

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.075
and then you can't get back out.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.577
[grunts]

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.514
Can I just stay here?

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.148
Sure.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.450
See you later.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.719
Bear, this is-- you
can't leave me for dead.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:31.291
I have a number of stand-up
dates at some pretty

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:35.295
prominent local casinos.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.729
Keep going, Joel.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:37.897
Keep moving.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.500
OK, I'm coming through.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.868
I'm all right.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.369
I'm fine.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.838
OK, hey, we did it.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:45.905
Yeah, looking good.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.440
Piece of cake.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:51.144
Yes, piece of cake, a very
thinly sliced piece of cake.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.446
JOEL MCHALE: Bear, he--

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.815
he just runs off, and
then I have to catch

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.116
up with him all the time.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.184
I guess that's how it
works on this show.

